<p>Strikes across Ukraine, Russian-occupied territory and Russia killed at least 16 people over the past day, according to officials cited by multiple outlets. Some of the dead were reported in Dnipro and Sevastopol. The attacks came as the region marked the 40th anniversary of the 1986 Chernobyl nuclear disaster, renewing attention to the risks of military activity around nuclear sites during Russia’s more than four-year war against Ukraine. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky used the anniversary to warn that Russian actions could recreate nuclear danger, while the day’s violence showed again that the conflict continues to hit Ukrainian and Russian-held areas, as well as Russia itself.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/uFuo6VC-v0MpruqihyXbIQlJm2CcgtSzjZsuuwarGGXzpnm2Vrd2e3OHMK8MosFW2d2hiDDWCB7PeKHcsrmJKB6a1O6YedHoH0v3O0zqldJY0-FqHEzwj1IP5zTxHj9kQ4p1KDw92N-LWC9SUDdFtIX_bGrhgK_nwEvgTG1Msw8lc4IgJqEd3nCin-2Zu17UbtdG2nJr-D3yA04ToWB7Dnmg-wWa7YdID-IEoa2G6hrruzvhYvo3rGN6vpmMbFPFef2nOBq4lYRCQ_3Zkw' alt='Russian Emergency Ministry troops and veterans lay flowers at the graves of firefighters at the Mitinskoye Cemetery where several victims of the Chernobyl nuclear disaster are buried, marking the 40th anniversary of the explosion and fire at the Chernobyl nuclear power plant in Ukraine, outside Moscow, Sunday, April 26, 2026. (AP Photo/Alexander Zemlianichenko)' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Dnipro toll: Russian drone and missile strikes on Dnipro killed at least nine people, Ukrainian authorities said, making it one of the deadliest single-city attacks reported in the latest exchange.</li><li>Sevastopol strike: Russian officials said a Ukrainian drone strike on the port city of Sevastopol killed one man, showing that the hostilities also reached Crimea on the anniversary weekend.</li><li>Nuclear warning: The anniversary sharpened concern over attacks near the Chernobyl site, with coverage emphasizing that fighting around nuclear facilities can revive fears far beyond the battlefield.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Volodymyr Zelensky: Ukraine’s president marked the Chernobyl anniversary by warning that Russian attacks are reviving the danger of a nuclear catastrophe, using the date to stress the war’s wider global stakes. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/russia-central-asia/article/3351499/16-dead-strikes-chernobyl-anniversary-highlights-nuclear-risks-russia-ukraine-war'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Ukrainian authorities: Officials in Ukraine highlighted the human cost in Dnipro, where they said Russian drone and missile strikes killed at least nine people in the latest attacks. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/27/at-least-16-killed-across-ukraine-and-russia-in-exhange-of-strikes-on-chernobyl-anniversar'>Euronews</a>)</li><li>Russian officials: Authorities on the Russian side said a Ukrainian drone strike killed one man in Sevastopol, underscoring Moscow’s position that Russian territory and Russian-held areas are also under attack. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/27/at-least-16-killed-across-ukraine-and-russia-in-exhange-of-strikes-on-chernobyl-anniversar'>Euronews</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/strikes-ukraine-russia-kill-16-chernobyl-anniversary-132394862'>Strikes in Ukraine and Russia kill at least 16 on Chernobyl anniversary</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/russia-central-asia/article/3351499/16-dead-strikes-chernobyl-anniversary-highlights-nuclear-risks-russia-ukraine-war'>Strikes in Ukraine and Russia kill at least 16 on Chernobyl disaster anniversary</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/ukraine-russian-attacks-chernobyl-anniversary/'>At least 16 dead in strikes across Ukraine and Russia on Chernobyl anniversary</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-ukraine-russia-strikes-on-chernobyl-anniversary/'>Strikes in U